,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"}]}},"dossier":{"summary":{"summary":"Hammersmith and Fulham borrowed a further \u00a335m from the PWLB and repaid \u00a316m in 2024/25, lifting debt from \u00a3269.2m to \u00a3288.3m (all fixed rate, average 3.75%), with 82.4% of the debt serviced by the housing account. The striking move is on the other side of the balance sheet: cash invested fell 72% in the year, from \u00a3159.3m to \u00a344.2m, all now held short-term in money market funds and one \u00a310m local-authority deposit. The total CFR rose from \u00a3614m to \u00a3766.7m, so the council is heavily under-borrowed (HRA internal borrowing alone is \u00a3222m) and future capital spend implies substantial further borrowing. All prudential indicators were met, with only 2% of debt maturing within 12 months, and the figures remain subject to external audit.","fy":"2024/25","as_of_doc":"Treasury Management Outturn Report 2024/25","as_of_url":"https://lbhf.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s132645/Treasury Management Outturn Report 202425.pdf","as_of_date":"2025-10-27","signals":[{"code":"borrowing-increase","headline":"Debt up \u00a319.1m to \u00a3288.3m in 2024/25 (\u00a335m new PWLB less \u00a316m repaid) while total CFR rose \u00a3152.7m to \u00a3766.7m","why":"The gap between a \u00a3767m borrowing need and \u00a3288m actual debt is a pipeline of future borrowing at today's higher rates."},{"code":"low-liquidity","headline":"Cash invested fell from \u00a3159.3m to \u00a344.2m during 2024/25, all short-term, against \u00a3288.3m debt and \u00a3235m in-year capital spend","why":"A \u00a3115m cash rundown in one year leaves a thin buffer and points to external borrowing or further drawdown ahead."}],"key_figures":[{"name":"borrowing","value":"\u00a3288.3m at 3.75% average (GF \u00a350.9m, HRA \u00a3237.4m), up from \u00a3269.2m at 3.72%; all fixed rate","as_at":"31/3/25","page":3},{"name":"investments","value":"\u00a344.2m short-term (\u00a334.2m MMFs, \u00a310m local-authority term d